This commit introduces the vulnerable behavior described in the root cause. Specifically, it adds the logic to dynamically clear the RTF_ADDRCONF flag from an existing route (iter) when a new route (rt) without this flag is added: 

+ if (!(rt->fib6_flags & (RTF_ADDRCONF | RTF_PREFIX_RT))) {
+ iter->fib6_flags &= ~RTF_ADDRCONF;
+ iter->fib6_flags &= ~RTF_PREFIX_RT;
+ }

Clearing RTF_ADDRCONF dynamically makes the route eligible for ECMP, leading to a mismatch in the sibling count because the route was never registered in the fib6_siblings list.
